notes.body:
This works as is, though it seems doing both `redissectPackets()` and `cf_reload()` causes it to redissect all of the packets twice. Once when `redissectPackets()` is called directly and then once again when the reload finished event triggers `PacketList::captureFileReadFinished()`.

I'm currently experimenting with changing it to not directly trigger the redissection before reloading, though then it's necessary to trigger some of the work that `redissectPackets()` and it makes me uncomfortable thinking about the deferred processing with the `dissectIdle()` timing vs when we call `proto_free_deregistered_fields()`.

```c
    if (filehandler_name) {
        // Reload the file in case the FileHandler has changed
        cf_reload(cf);
        main_ui_->statusBar->expertUpdate();
        proto_free_deregistered_fields();
    } else {
        // 
        redissectPackets();
    }
```

